# overload_resolve.tkr — §9 A method/function overloading, exercised end to end (definition,
# call-site selection, and the per-overload symbol suffix) through one witness number.
#
# The witness reads back which body ran, in arithmetic only the correct resolution produces:
#   A1 by-type:      area(3) = 9,  area(3.0) = 109
#   A2 by-name:      mk(width := 5) = 10,  mk(height := 5) = 15   (identical types, name discriminates)
#   A3 exact>widen:  pick(a: i32) = 1   (never the i64 overload's 2, never ambiguous)
#   A4 cast:         cast_pick(0 to u32) = 7
# Sum = 9 + 109 + 10 + 15 + 1 + 7 = 151. A relapse in any path moves the total off 151.

Feature: overload_resolve — a call selects exactly one overload, and each overload keeps its own body

  Scenario: type, name, exact-over-widening, and cast resolution all reach the correct bodies
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "151"
